This project is a simulation of a PLC-controlled bottle filling production line.
The system is designed to simulate how conveyors in a small industrial plant operate in a sequential and safe manner.

The production line contains three conveyor belts and two control push buttons:

Start Button
Stop Button

- (System Operation)

When the Start button is pressed:

1-The first conveyor starts running.
2-After a 10-second delay using a timer, the second conveyor starts.
3-After another 10 seconds, the third conveyor starts.

The delay between each conveyor represents the time required for the bottles to move safely from one conveyor to the next until they reach the end of the production line.

- When the Stop button is pressed:

1-The third conveyor stops first.
2-Then the second conveyor stops after a delay.
3-Finally, the first conveyor stops.

This reverse shutdown sequence helps prevent bottle accumulation and keeps the system operating safely and smoothly.

Project Goal

The purpose of this project is to demonstrate:

.PLC sequential control logic
.Timer instructions
.Industrial conveyor automation
.Safe startup and shutdown procedures in manufacturing systems
